# Convoy's own first-run writes these into every seat worktree (CANON:
# ensure_first_run writes an AGENTS.md pointer and the hook files; earlier
# versions also wrote skill copies under .grok/.claude/.agents). A checkout of
# this repository can itself be a seat worktree, so here they are generated
# artifacts, not repo content. If a curated AGENTS.md is ever wanted, `git add -f` it.
.claude/
.grok/
.codex/
.agents/skills/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Durable-root fixtures for index prune tests (must sit outside OS temp).
test/demo/_keep_roots/

# Per-seat thread pointer / handoff layer written into a checkout.
.ola/
thread.md

# Per-session operator notes (seed / handoff prompts). Machine-specific paths,
# never repo content.
SEED.md
PRIOR_THREAD.md

# Conductor/neuron message drops that live untracked in a seat checkout.
CHIP.md
/CONDUCTOR*.md
CONFIRM.md
GREEN.md
LATENCY.md
LIVE_SEAT_SPEC.md
ORCH_SEND.md
PUSH.md
STAMP.md
ULTRACODE.md
# secrets and pairing records never belong in git
*.token
conductors.jsonl
tenants.jsonl
origin.json

# Working briefs: task assignments to agents on a given day, not documentation.
